<h3 id="whatsapp-business-app"><b>WhatsApp Business App</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A </span><a href="https://business.whatsapp.com/products/business-app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp Business App</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> offered directly by Meta at no cost, particularly for companies. You can target a limited number of potential customers using the application. The WhatsApp Business App allows you to broadcast up to 256 contacts at once. To </span><a href="/resources/blog/how-to-send-bulk-messages-on-whatsapp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">send bulk messages</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, you can either create a group or broadcast messages. Using the app is restricted in terms of scalability and automation, and is only perfect for small businesses with low communication needs.</span></p>
<h3 id="bulk-whatsapp-message-sender"><b>Bulk WhatsApp Message Sender</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are so many unverified bulk WhatsApp message sender tools available in the market. The tool does not use the official API. Rather, they operate using Chrome extensions or desktop apps on top of WhatsApp web. This could be a reason for getting your WhatsApp number banned due to non-compliance with WhatsApp’s policies.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To avoid these risks, choose a </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-bulk-message-senders/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">verified WhatsApp Bulk Message Sender</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> instead. They follow WhatsApp’s rules and protect your number from bans.</span></p>
